---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import PriceTier from '../components/PriceTier.astro';
import BookingBlock from '../components/BookingBlock.astro';
import ProvisionalNote from '../components/ProvisionalNote.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
import { PRICING } from '../consts';
import {
  TIER_INTRO,
  TIER_INITIAL,
  TIER_FOLLOW_UP,
} from '../data/approved-copy';

const title = 'Consultations';
const description =
  'A private space to talk through what you are actually facing, with a pediatric nurse practitioner and lactation consultant. Start with a free 15-minute call.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Section narrow>
    <p class="eyebrow">Consultations</p>
    <h1>Bring your situation, and we'll work through it together.</h1>
    <p class="lede__sub">
      A private space to talk through what you're actually facing — the
      emotional and psychological side of caring for a young child, held with
      both clinical experience and faith.
    </p>
    <p class="lede__cta">
      {/* §4.2: the $250 initial is a significant ask cold. The free call is
          the real conversion event, so it is the primary CTA on this page. */}
      <Button href="#book">Book a free 15-minute call</Button>
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tint narrow labelledby="what-heading">
    <h2 id="what-heading">What a session is like</h2>
    <p>
      We meet on Zoom or FaceTime, wherever you are, with your baby on you if
      that's how the hour has to go. You talk, and I listen properly — not to
      the first minute of it while I decide what to tell you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Then we work through it. Sometimes that's untangling what's actually
      happening from what you've been told is happening. Sometimes it's
      permission to stop doing something that isn't working. Often it's both,
      and often the thing underneath is not the thing you booked about.
    </p>
    <p>
      You'll leave with something you can do this week, not a reading list.
    </p>

    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <p>
      Parents and parents-to-be, and anyone else doing the caring — aunts and
      uncles, grandparents, teachers, students, and care providers. Families
      and new parents are welcome to book together; that's the same
      consultation, not a different product.
    </p>
    <p>
      You do not need to arrive with a crisis, and you do not need to have
      tried everything first.
    </p>

    <ProvisionalNote pending="the client's licensing board or attorney review">
      <p>
        Noorture consultations are consultation and education. They are not
        medical care, do not create a provider–patient relationship, and are
        not a substitute for care from your own clinician. If something is
        urgent, contact your doctor or your local emergency service.
      </p>
      <p>
        Hoda is a licensed nurse practitioner. Whether a given consultation can
        be offered depends on where you are located.
      </p>
    </ProvisionalNote>
  </Section>

  <Section labelledby="pricing-heading">
    <h2 id="pricing-heading" class="section-heading">The three tiers</h2>

    <div class="tiers">
      <PriceTier
        name="Introductory call"
        price={PRICING.consultIntro.label}
        meta={`${PRICING.consultIntro.minutes} minutes · Zoom or FaceTime`}
        href="#book"
        ctaLabel="Book the free call"
        featured
      >
        {/* CLIENT-APPROVED, VERBATIM (§4.2). See approved-copy.json. */}
        <p>{TIER_INTRO}</p>
      </PriceTier>

      <PriceTier
        name="Initial consultation"
        price={PRICING.consultInitial.label}
        meta={`${PRICING.consultInitial.minutes} minutes · Zoom or FaceTime`}
        href="#book"
        ctaLabel="Request a time"
      >
        {/* CLIENT-APPROVED, VERBATIM (§4.2). See approved-copy.json. */}
        <p>{TIER_INITIAL}</p>
      </PriceTier>

      <PriceTier
        name="Follow-up"
        price={PRICING.consultFollowUp.label}
        meta={`${PRICING.consultFollowUp.minutes} minutes · Zoom or FaceTime`}
        href="#book"
        ctaLabel="Request a time"
      >
        {/* CLIENT-APPROVED, VERBATIM (§4.2). See approved-copy.json. */}
        <p>{TIER_FOLLOW_UP}</p>
      </PriceTier>
    </div>

    <p class="tiers__note">
      Looking for a taught session on one topic instead — birth, breastfeeding,
      bonding? That's a <a href="/private-class">Private Class</a>. In a
      consultation you bring the situation; in a class, Hoda brings the
      curriculum.
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section tint>
    <BookingBlock
      product="consultation"
      intro="Tell me a little about what's going on and when you're usually free. I'll come back with times."
      options={[
        { value: 'intro', label: `Free ${PRICING.consultIntro.minutes}-minute introductory call` },
        { value: 'initial', label: `Initial consultation — ${PRICING.consultInitial.minutes} minutes, ${PRICING.consultInitial.label}` },
        { value: 'follow-up', label: `Follow-up — ${PRICING.consultFollowUp.minutes} minutes, ${PRICING.consultFollowUp.label}` },
        { value: 'unsure', label: "Not sure yet — let's talk" },
      ]}
    />
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-noor-rose-ink);
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
  }

  .lede__sub {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-noor-ink-soft);
  }

  .lede__cta {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.85rem;
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
  }
  h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }

  .section-heading {
    margin: 0 0 clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    text-align: center;
  }

  .tiers {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .tiers__note {
    margin: 2rem auto 0;
    max-width: 38rem;
    text-align: center;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-noor-ink-soft);
  }
  .tiers__note a {
    color: var(--color-noor-aqua-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .tiers {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
